From c465e68130e1f667914f5d1887f95dac51655651 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Thompson <brandon.joseph.thompson@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 08:59:25 -0700
Subject: Patch: Apply 12/24-hour format everywhere, move toggle to Desktop >
 General.

Adapted for beta-18: the Hub is now schema-driven (SchemaPage + a
rows.js per page, loaded by URL through Hub.qml's pageFile map) rather
than one big hand-wired ShellSettingsPage.qml, so General is a new
schema (schema/GeneralPage.js) + thin page (pages/GeneralPage.qml)
wired into Hub.qml's groups/jpName/sectionKeywords/searchIndex/
framedSet/ledgerSet/pageFile/defs/srcOf/adapterFor/fileFor/save/diff --
all the places a schema-backed section touches, mirrored from how
"shell" already does it. A new hub/quickshell/Singletons/Config.qml
singleton (registered in that dir's qmldir) gives the Hub's own
WidgetsPage live preview read access to the shared clock24h, same
pattern as the pill/launcher/widgets Config singletons.

Also wired general.json into the Go backend's rice (settings-sharing)
system as a fourth wholesale-captured store (rice.go), which doesn't
exist on main -- without it, moving clock24h out of widgets.json would
have silently dropped it from a shared rice, since general.json was
invisible to capture/apply/preflight.

Extended past the original patch's scope to three bar styles that
didn't exist when it was written (dyad, washi, atoll's calendar
popout), each with their own hardcoded HH:mm clock -- otherwise "every
clock in the shell" would leave three of them out. Left
NotesWidget.qml's HH:mm alone: that's a note's edited-at timestamp,
not a clock face.
